From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:07:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Complete inventory traversal before servicing soft refresh
 requests

Accepted local transactions and successful peer activations used the same zero deadline as hard context invalidation. Repeated soft events consequently rebuilt the cached inventory from index zero every turn, starving higher-indexed transactions.

Record a bounded pending refresh flag for those two soft events. Finish the existing four-item pages, then immediately rebuild so new peers revisit the prefix and newly accepted entries enter the next snapshot. Preserve immediate tip and authority invalidation, the 1000-identity snapshot bound, and output backpressure. Keep the explicitly supported local relay-required policy and clarify its distinction from optional protocol negotiation.

The new isolated regression compiles the actual helper, soft-event assignments and Run snapshot/cursor block against bounded identity/output adapters. It fails against cd8d5140ec with steady-submission tail starvation and passes after repair, covering peer churn, prefix revisit, eventual snapshot inclusion, finite backpressure and hard fences. The existing relay-output regression also passes. This is scheduler evidence, not pool validation or live network acceptance; no full build or nodes ran.
